 "title": "HR vs Candidate Salary Negotiation Roleplay",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "A roleplay demonstration between an HR manager and a candidate negotiating a salary. The candidate has 7.5 years of experience, a current CTC of 9,20,000, and negotiates up to a final offer of 12.5 LPA.",
 "key_points": [
  "Candidate total experience: 7.5 years all into R2R.",
  "Notice period: 30 days.",
  "Current CTC: 9,20,000.",
  "Candidate expectation: 13 to 14 LPA (around 50-60 percent hike) wanting to upskill on GenAI and stay long-term.",
  "Current in-hand salary after deductions: 72,000 per month.",
  "Candidate goal in next company: minimum 1,10,000 in-hand after deductions.",
  "HR counter-offer range: 11 to 13 LPA.",
  "Candidate lowest acceptable counter-offer: 12.5 LPA.",
  "Final agreed compensation: 12.5 LPA."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by Smalltalk. Text / caption: Every job seeker has a story, every interview creates an opportunity, and every job opens a new door. #smalltalk #jobseeker #recruitment #humanresource #interview. Transcript: Hello. Ah yes sir, please tell. So what is the total years of experience you are having? It's almost like 7.5. All into same domain? All into R2R. What is the notice period here? 30 days. And CTC? It's 9 lakh 20,000. Okay. Expectation? Expecting something between 13 to 14. 13 to 14 is nearly 50 60 percent hike I am mentioning. Ah because I am looking for a long term staying in a company. Valid valid point. But can you please help me understand what you are basing your expected CTC on? I mean you are going with the current market range or the current drawn salary or you are having any competitive offer in hand right now? More like what is the current market value that has for for an experience candidate and that to like upskill myself on the GenAI part. Ok. Ok so completely empathetic towards your ask. I just want to know ok let me put it this way. If this role or opportunity you find it a good fit, what will be the compensation range you will seriously considering? See now currently after all the deductions I am getting 72k in hand okay. So my goal is to get minimum like 1,10,000 in my next company after all the deductions is. But based on current market range for the similar profiles your ask is on bit on higher side. So would you open to consider for a compensation range around 11 to 13 LPA? 11 is just like 2 lakhs increase in my current package. So 11 would be very less. I can go till 12.5 not less than that. Great sounds good. 12.5 we can consider. Okay. Yes sure. Thank you. Thank you for your time. Thank you so much.",
